1
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:05,535
The only blockchain use case

2
00:00:05,535 --> 00:00:08,400
that really found real-world use is financial applications.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:09,800
For retail users.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,277
This is another option for them

5
00:00:11,277 --> 00:00:12,700
to get into the capital markets.

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,500
Traditional way, it was real estate.

7
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:15,350
Stock trading.

8
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:16,400
Futures trading, options.

9
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:16,700
Right?

10
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:17,521
All these good stuff.

11
00:00:17,521 --> 00:00:18,100
They are great.

12
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:20,914
But the legacy market that we are using today

13
00:00:20,914 --> 00:00:23,495
is actually not fair to the retail audience

14
00:00:23,495 --> 00:00:26,137
because the edge that you have on the trade

15
00:00:26,137 --> 00:00:27,734
comes not from information.

16
00:00:27,734 --> 00:00:31,356
It actually comes from how close you are to the data center.

17
00:00:31,506 --> 00:00:33,756
So that's an unfair playing field for people.
